<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01KF">Definition <span data-tag="01KF">4.6.4.1</span> <span class="named">(The Oriented Fiber Product)</span>.</a> Let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ and $G: \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ be morphisms of simplicial sets. We let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\vec{\times }_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ denote the simplicial set given by the iterated fiber product </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\times _{ \operatorname{Fun}( \{ 0\} , \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) } \operatorname{Fun}( \Delta ^1, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) \times _{ \operatorname{Fun}(\{ 1\} , \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) } \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}. \]
</div>
<p> We will refer to $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\vec{\times }_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ as the <em>oriented fiber product</em> of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ with $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ over $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$. </p>
</article>
